  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice recently converted all the positive integers from 111 to 2N−12^N - 12N−1 (both inclusive) into binary strings and stored them in an array SSS.  Note that the binary strings **do not have leading zeroes**.\n\nWhile she was out, Bob **sorted** all the elements of SSS in lexicographical increasing order.\n\nLet SiS_iSi​ denotes the ithi^{th}ith string in the **sorted array**.\n\nAlice defined a function FFF such that F(Si)F(S_i)F(Si​) is equal to the count of 111 in the string SiS_iSi​.\n\nFor example, F(101)=2F(101) = 2F(101)=2 and F(1000)=1F(1000) = 1F(1000)=1.\n\nGiven a positive integer KKK, find the value of ∑i=1KF(Si)\\sum_{i = 1}^K F(S_i)∑i=1K​F(Si​).\n\nString PPP is lexicographically smaller than string QQQ if one of the following satisfies:\n\n\nPPP is a prefix of QQQ and P≠QP \\neq QP=Q.\nThere exists an index iii such that Pi&lt;QiP_i &lt; Q_iPi​&lt;Qi​ and for all j&lt;ij &lt; ij&lt;i,  Pj=QjP_j=Q_jPj​=Qj​.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain an integer TTT - number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the value ∑i=1KF(Si)\\sum_{i = 1}^K F(S_i)∑i=1K​F(Si​).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤30001 \\leq T \\leq 30001≤T≤3000",
      "1≤N≤501 \\leq N \\leq 501≤N≤50",
      "1≤K≤2N−11 \\leq K \\leq 2^N - 11≤K≤2N−1",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 2\n3 4\n3 7",
        "output": "2\n5\n12",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nConverting positive integers to Binary Strings:\n\n1=11 = 11=1\n2=102 = 102=10\n3=113 = 113=11\n4=1004 = 1004=100\n5=1015 = 1015=101\n6=1106 = 1106=110\n7=1117 = 1117=111\n\nSorting Binary Strings in lexicographical order:\nAfter sorting, the strings will appear in the following order:\n[1,10,100,101,11,110,111][1, 10, 100, 101, 11, 110, 111][1,10,100,101,11,110,111].\nTest case 111: F(S1)+F(S2)=F(1)+F(10)=1+1=2F(S_1) + F(S_2) = F(1) + F(10) = 1 + 1 = 2F(S1​)+F(S2​)=F(1)+F(10)=1+1=2.\nTest case 222: F(S1)+F(S2)+F(S3)+F(S4)=F(1)+F(10)+F(100)+F(101)=1+1+1+2=5F(S_1) + F(S_2) + F(S_3) + F(S_4) = F(1) + F(10) + F(100) + F(101) = 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 5F(S1​)+F(S2​)+F(S3​)+F(S4​)=F(1)+F(10)+F(100)+F(101)=1+1+1+2=5."
      }
    ]
  },
